@startuml 04-sequence-task-lifecycle
title FlowAI Platform - Task Lifecycle (sequence)

autonumber

participant "Automation" as Auto
participant "Operator (UI)" as U
participant "API Gateway" as GW
participant "Source Queue" as qsrc
participant "Event Router" as ER
participant "Executor Queue" as qexec
participant "Executor" as EX
participant "Agent Container" as AG
participant "Event Fanout Queue" as qevt
participant "LLM Provider" as LLM

note over Auto, U
  Automation submits via API Gateway. Operator observes via WS and can intervene.
  Event Router is a pure queue take-and-put service: no business logic, no DB.
end note

== Submit ==

Auto -> GW : POST /tasks (prompt, tools, secret_ids)
GW -> GW : Build scope (HMAC: project, task, secret_ids, TTL)
GW -> GW : Persist task
GW -> qsrc : enqueue task (LPUSH)
GW --> Auto : 202 task_id

U -> GW : WS connect (subscribe to task events)

== Dispatch (event-router take-and-put) ==

ER -> qsrc : pull next task (BLPOP / SUBSCRIBE)
ER -> ER : resolve target executor via routing rules
ER -> qexec : put on per-executor queue
ER --> EX : poll q:exec-X -> deliver task_spec + scope_token (one-shot handoff)
EX -> EX : Pull image
EX -> AG : Start container, inject secrets as env / tmpfs

note over AG, EX
  Agent is a black box. Runs initial instructions. No platform API.
end note

AG -> LLM : Prompt + history
LLM --> AG : Completion or tool_use

== Agent loop (event fanout) ==

loop agent loop
  AG --> EX : stdout (event stream)
  EX -> qevt : publish events (task_id, kind, payload)
  ER -> qevt : consume events
  ER -> qevt : put on fanout queue (per task subscription)
  GW -> qevt : subscribe, forward to WS clients
  GW --> U : WS push (live)

  opt Operator intervenes
    U -> GW : inject message / cancel / rerun
    GW -> ER : forward control event
    ER -> qexec : put control event on executor queue
    EX -> qexec : poll -> receive control event
    EX --> AG : forward (or stop)
  end

  AG -> LLM : Next prompt
  LLM --> AG : Next completion
end

== Finalize ==

AG --> EX : final result (stdout / exit code)
EX -> qevt : publish final event (status)
ER -> qevt : consume final
ER -> GW : forward final
GW -> GW : UPDATE state to terminal
GW --> Auto : webhook / status (if configured)
GW --> U : WS final

note over AG, EX
  Container terminated. Scope token expires.
end note

@enduml